44:22.020 --> 44:22.440
Exactly.

44:22.440 --> 44:23.960
So, that was the

44:23.960 --> 44:24.700
strict graph.

44:24.920 --> 44:25.580
It found six

44:25.580 --> 44:26.780
highly specific but

44:26.780 --> 44:28.240
conditional paths.

44:29.000 --> 44:29.960
But then, the author

44:29.960 --> 44:30.820
introduces the

44:30.820 --> 44:32.320
matched graph.

44:33.100 --> 44:33.720
And the results of

44:33.720 --> 44:34.780
this test completely

44:34.780 --> 44:35.440
inverted my

44:35.440 --> 44:35.980
expectations.

44:36.320 --> 44:37.580
So, what does this

44:37.580 --> 44:37.900
all mean?

44:38.080 --> 44:38.980
Let's get into this,

44:39.200 --> 44:40.080
because this is where

44:40.080 --> 44:41.220
the reality of dynamic

44:41.220 --> 44:42.300
languages really

44:42.300 --> 44:43.140
rears its head.

44:44.380 --> 44:45.260
What did the

44:45.260 --> 44:46.280
matched graph do

44:46.280 --> 44:46.880
differently?

44:47.320 --> 44:48.600
The matched graph

44:48.600 --> 44:49.540
attempts to solve

44:49.540 --> 44:50.420
the problem of

44:50.420 --> 44:51.880
unresolved calls that

44:51.880 --> 44:52.720
the strict graph

44:52.720 --> 44:53.060
ignored.

44:53.540 --> 44:54.700
In Python, you

44:54.700 --> 44:55.760
often see code that

44:55.760 --> 44:57.100
just says, call the

44:57.100 --> 44:58.080
update method on

44:58.080 --> 44:58.640
this object.

44:59.220 --> 45:00.200
But, statically,

45:00.440 --> 45:01.340
without running the

45:01.340 --> 45:02.280
code, the parser

45:02.280 --> 45:02.880
doesn't know what

45:02.880 --> 45:03.800
class that object

45:03.800 --> 45:04.380
belongs to.

45:04.580 --> 45:05.000
Right, it could be

45:05.000 --> 45:05.300
anything.

45:06.300 --> 45:07.300
Is it a database

45:07.300 --> 45:08.540
object, a dictionary,

45:09.000 --> 45:09.820
a custom class?

45:10.300 --> 45:11.400
The strict graph

45:11.400 --> 45:12.400
dropped those.

45:13.060 --> 45:14.120
The matched graph,

45:14.200 --> 45:15.160
however, tried a

45:15.160 --> 45:16.120
heuristic approach.

45:16.380 --> 45:17.200
It linked them by

45:17.200 --> 45:17.580
name.

45:17.640 --> 45:18.100
Oh, boy.

45:18.340 --> 45:19.200
If it saw an

45:19.200 --> 45:20.340
unresolved call to a

45:20.340 --> 45:20.960
method named

45:20.960 --> 45:22.700
