45:22.700 --> 45:23.360
drew an edge to

45:23.360 --> 45:23.980
every single

45:23.980 --> 45:24.720
analyzed method

45:24.720 --> 45:25.200
named update

45:25.200 --> 45:25.960
across the entire

45:25.960 --> 45:26.500
project.

45:27.140 --> 45:27.780
That sounds like a

45:27.780 --> 45:29.180
recipe for absolute

45:29.180 --> 45:29.920
chaos.

45:30.440 --> 45:31.220
Update is probably

45:31.220 --> 45:32.000
one of the most

45:32.000 --> 45:33.460
common programming

45:33.460 --> 45:34.580
verbs in existence.

45:35.000 --> 45:36.060
It was an explosion.

45:36.480 --> 45:37.520
Suddenly, the graph

45:37.520 --> 45:38.260
ballooned.

45:38.580 --> 45:39.740
The K-ratio shot up

45:39.740 --> 45:41.260
to 11.87,

45:41.640 --> 45:43.100
massively supercritical.

45:43.300 --> 45:43.520
Wow.

45:43.520 --> 45:44.800
And instead of six

45:44.800 --> 45:45.800
entry points having a

45:45.800 --> 45:46.740
witness path to a

45:46.740 --> 45:50.020
