45:51.400 --> 45:52.080
Wait, really?

45:52.300 --> 45:52.480
Yeah.

45:53.040 --> 45:53.560
207?

45:53.560 --> 45:54.760
That's almost half the

45:54.760 --> 45:55.520
entry points in the

45:55.520 --> 45:55.920
library.

45:56.160 --> 45:57.380
Was the software really

45:57.380 --> 45:58.080
that fundamentally

45:58.080 --> 45:58.460
broken?

45:58.760 --> 45:59.920
No, and that's the

45:59.920 --> 46:00.620
crucial lesson.

46:00.880 --> 46:01.140
Okay.

46:01.820 --> 46:02.840
The author reveals a

46:02.840 --> 46:04.380
glaring false positive to

46:04.380 --> 46:05.740
demonstrate exactly why

46:05.740 --> 46:06.920
this explosion happened.

46:07.260 --> 46:08.140
Okay, let's hear it.

46:08.140 --> 46:09.300
In the dependency

46:09.300 --> 46:11.540
git-db, there was a

46:11.540 --> 46:13.260
basic write method that

46:13.260 --> 46:14.380
called an update method

46:14.380 --> 46:15.540
on a local, harmless

46:15.540 --> 46:16.400
hash object.

46:16.900 --> 46:17.720
Because of the

46:17.720 --> 46:18.720
aggressive rules of

46:18.720 --> 46:20.660
the matched graph, that

46:20.660 --> 46:21.780
call got mistakenly

46:21.780 --> 46:22.760
linked to a completely

46:22.760 --> 46:24.120
unrelated, highly

46:24.120 --> 46:25.560
sensitive update method

46:25.560 --> 46:26.880
in the main git-python

46:26.880 --> 46:28.440
application, simply

46:28.440 --> 46:29.280
because they shared the

46:29.280 --> 46:30.620
exact same English word

46:30.620 --> 46:31.200
as a name.

46:31.460 --> 46:32.020
It was a complete

46:32.020 --> 46:32.840
hallucination.

46:33.320 --> 46:33.940
A structural

46:33.940 --> 46:35.300
hallucination caused by

46:35.300 --> 46:36.020
the mapmaker's

46:36.020 --> 46:36.380
assumptions.

46:36.380 --> 46:38.440
That is such a vital

46:38.440 --> 46:39.260
insight for anyone

46:39.260 --> 46:40.040
building or buying

46:40.040 --> 46:40.780
security tools.

46:40.920 --> 46:41.500
It shows the

46:41.500 --> 46:42.760
incredible, almost

46:42.760 --> 46:43.800
dangerous sensitivity

46:43.800 --> 46:45.160
of structural screens

46:45.160 --> 46:46.140
to how you extract the

46:46.140 --> 46:46.740
data in the first

46:46.740 --> 46:47.060
place.

46:47.340 --> 46:47.920
It really does.

46:48.440 --> 46:49.240
If you use a strict

46:49.240 --> 46:49.900
graph, you have

46:49.900 --> 46:51.120
terrifying blind spots.

46:51.260 --> 46:52.020
You might miss a

46:52.020 --> 46:53.280
